{
  "requirement": "`Criterion::execute` can compute an answer without a configured model provider.\nA criterion can compute its answer directly using tracked inputs; deterministic\nexecution needs no configured agent. Evidence storage is still required.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.validation.deterministic_procedures`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the requirement**\n1. `Criterion::execute` computes an answer with no model provider or agent configured.\n2. A criterion computes its answer directly from tracked inputs.\n3. Evidence storage is still required and still works for such a criterion.\n\n**Coverage**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` covers all three obligations.\n  - It builds `Validator::new(graph.clone())` with no `with_agent` call. `Validator::new` sets `agent: None` and `renderer: None`.\n  - The `Review` criterion's `execute` reads the node through `ctx.inspection().read(...)` and never calls an agent. This is the tracked-input computation.\n  - The test asserts `!result.output().result` and `rationale == \"ordinary computation\"`, so the answer is computed from the node contents.\n  - It calls `store_evidence`, reloads the record with `load_evidence`, and asserts the stored dependency is `Dependency::Node(Node(1), fingerprint)` with the fingerprint value `\"ordinary computation\"`. This shows evidence storage is required and used, and that the inputs were tracked.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` uses an agentless `Validator::new(domain)`. It asserts the typed output, that execution alone does not write, and that `store_evidence` persists records. It covers execution plus storage across several criteria.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` also uses an agentless validator. It covers executing, storing, reloading and re-checking a deterministic answer.\n\n**Gaps**\nNone found. The mapping to the requirement's three obligations is direct, and the assertions check outputs, stored records and dependencies rather than just running the code. The agent-configured tests in `agent.rs` are outside this requirement.",
  "references": "74175acba8689023c8181e2be9ff3366b370ca066f284bc203555f8206920b71",
